Subject: [PATCH sched_ext/for-7.3-fixes 0/2] sched_ext: Fix two cid bugs that can crash the kernel or block loading
To: Tejun Heo <tj@kernel.org>
Cc: David Vernet <void@manifault.com>,
    Andrea Righi <arighi@nvidia.com>,
    Changwoo Min <changwoo@igalia.com>,
    Ching-Chun Huang <jserv@ccns.ncku.edu.tw>,
    Chia-Ping Tsai <chia7712@gmail.com>,
    sched-ext@lists.linux.dev,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

Two independent fixes for cid code that is already in mainline (v7.2).
Neither depends on the other.

  1: The kernel keeps three cmasks in the BPF scheduler's arena (the
     per-cpu set_cmask scratch, the online cid mask and the
     sub_caps_updated output). The BPF scheduler can free those pages
     with bpf_arena_free_pages(), and the next kernel write to them
     (a set_cpumask, a hotplug event, a caps update) oopses the kernel.
     Access them with copy_{from,to}_kernel_nofault() instead and abort
     the scheduler with scx_error() when the pages are gone.

  2: When cacheinfo detection fails for a CPU, its LLC shared_cpu_map is
     empty, scx_cid_init() hits a WARN and returns -EINVAL, and no
     scheduler can be loaded, cpu-form ones included. Use the LLC map
     only when cacheinfo is populated and contains the CPU, and fall
     back to the node mask otherwise.

Tested with vng on for-7.3-fixes. Without the patches, a BPF scheduler
that frees the set_cpumask scratch pages or the online cmask pages
panics the kernel from scx_call_op_set_cpumask() and handle_hotplug()
respectively, and forcing a cacheinfo failure on CPU 0 makes
scx_root_enable() fail with -22. With the patches, the first two only
abort the scheduler and the next one loads normally, and the third
loads using the node mask. The full selftests pass (nohz_tick skipped),
and scx_qmap with a sub-scheduler, affinity changes and CPU hotplug
runs without a BUG or WARN. The failure path in the sub-scheduler caps
update was checked by reading only.

The cacheinfo failure does not happen on x86 by itself; it was injected.
The realistic case is a DT or ACPI cacheinfo failure on arm64 or riscv.

checkpatch --strict is clean on both patches.

Cheng-Yang Chou (2):
  sched_ext: Don't oops when BPF frees the arena pages of kernel cmasks
  sched_ext: Fall back to the node mask when a CPU's LLC map is empty

